---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import PageHeader from '../components/PageHeader.astro';
import CtaBand from '../components/CtaBand.astro';
import Icon from '../components/Icon.astro';
import { site } from '../data/site';

const values = [
  {
    icon: 'target',
    title: 'Discipline',
    text: 'Nothing about this path was handed to me. Consistency, not luck, is what carried me from community college to leading engineering teams.',
  },
  {
    icon: 'compass',
    title: 'Identity',
    text: 'Knowing where I come from keeps me grounded. My heritage is not a side note to my career. It is the foundation under it.',
  },
  {
    icon: 'users',
    title: 'Service',
    text: 'I build for patients, workers, and communities, and I measure my work by whether it makes their lives easier.',
  },
  {
    icon: 'book-open',
    title: 'Education',
    text: 'Education changed my life. I want to open that same door for others as a mentor, educator, and community leader.',
  },
] as const;
---

<Base
  title="About"
  description="Sām Kazemi's story: from Antioch, California to Lead Software Engineer, and why he reclaimed his name and his Iranian heritage."
>
  <PageHeader
    eyebrow="About me"
    title="An engineer shaped by where he comes from"
    lead="Lead Software Engineer, SFSU computer science graduate, and a proud Iranian-American committed to advancing his community through education, cultural awareness, and advocacy."
  />

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container about">
      <aside class="about__aside reveal">
        <div class="name-card card">
          <p class="name-card__fa persian" lang="fa">{site.persianName}</p>
          <p class="name-card__en">{site.name}</p>
          <p class="name-card__note">Pronounced “Saam,” not short for Samuel.</p>
          <dl class="facts">
            <div>
              <dt><Icon name="map-pin" size={16} /> Roots</dt>
              <dd>Antioch, California</dd>
            </div>
            <div>
              <dt><Icon name="graduation-cap" size={16} /> Education</dt>
              <dd>B.S. Computer Science, SFSU · Minor in Persian Studies</dd>
            </div>
            <div>
              <dt><Icon name="briefcase" size={16} /> Now</dt>
              <dd>Lead Software Engineer, MedManage Solutions · Lead Engineer, Workforce Systems</dd>
            </div>
            <div>
              <dt><Icon name="languages" size={16} /> Languages</dt>
              <dd>English, Persian</dd>
            </div>
          </dl>
        </div>
      </aside>

      <div class="prose">
        <div class="reveal">
          <h2>Where I come from</h2>
          <p>
            I was born and raised in Antioch, California. Growing up, I watched gang violence take a
            real toll on friends and family, close enough to see how quickly a life can narrow when
            the options run out. That experience taught me early that nobody was going to hand me a
            way out. I would have to build one.
          </p>
          <p>
            I decided education would be that way out. I started at Los Medanos College in Pittsburg,
            made the Honor Roll while completing my lower-division computer science coursework, and
            transferred to San Francisco State University. In August 2026 I graduated with a B.S. in
            Computer Science, a 3.53 GPA, a place on the Dean’s List, and a minor in Persian Studies.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="reveal">
          <h2>Why computer science</h2>
          <p>
            I didn’t grow up around engineers. What changed my direction was watching a close friend
            build a successful career in software. It showed me, up close, what the field could make
            possible: financial stability, real opportunity, and the chance to break the cycle of
            poverty for yourself and your family. The more I learned about computing, the more I
            understood its reach, and I committed to it completely.
          </p>
          <p>
            That commitment turned into responsibility quickly. As Lead Software Engineer at
            MedManage Solutions, I architected <strong>ClearPath Virtual Health</strong> from the
            ground up: a HIPAA-compliant platform that helps care teams support patients living with
            chronic conditions. I lead its development, from scalable features and clinical
            workflows to a distributed engineering team. I’m also Lead Engineer at{' '}
            <strong>Workforce Systems</strong>, a startup building software for labor unions, where I
            design the platform and help secure contracts with the unions we serve.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="reveal">
          <h2>Why Sām</h2>
          <p>
            I was born Mojtaba Kazemi. As I studied Iranian history, I learned where that name came
            from and came to understand it as a slave name, one imposed on my people rather than
            drawn from our own culture. I chose to reclaim a name that is ours.
          </p>
          <blockquote>
            Sām is a name from Iran’s own epic tradition, carried by a hero of Ferdowsi’s{' '}
            <em>Shāhnāmeh</em>.
          </blockquote>
          <p>
            Sām (<span class="persian" lang="fa">سام</span>) is not a shortened Samuel. It is a
            Persian name with its own history, and carrying it is a daily reminder of who I am and
            who I answer to. You will still see “Mojtaba (Sām) Kazemi” on some official records.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="reveal">
          <h2>Heritage and community</h2>
          <p>
            My minor in Persian Studies was not a side interest. My long-term goal is to be an
            Iranocentric scholar, educator, and community leader: someone who helps Iranians,
            especially in the diaspora, know their history, language, and culture, and who advocates
            for them.
          </p>
          <p>
            I bring the same discipline to that mission that I bring to engineering. As a mentor in
            the MESA Program at San Francisco State, I help other students navigate academic and
            career decisions. I know firsthand how much one person showing you what’s possible can
            change your trajectory. My aim is to be that person for others, and to build success
            that is grounded in identity and values.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--alt">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-head section-head--center reveal">
        <p class="eyebrow">What I stand on</p>
        <h2>The values behind the work</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="grid grid--4">
        {
          values.map((v, i) => (
            <div class="card reveal" style={`--delay: ${i * 0.07}s`}>
              <span class="icon-badge">
                <Icon name={v.icon} />
              </span>
              <h3 class="value__title">{v.title}</h3>
              <p class="muted">{v.text}</p>
            </div>
          ))
        }
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <CtaBand />
</Base>

<style>
  .about {
    display: grid;
    gap: 48px;
  }

  @media (min-width: 960px) {
    .about {
      grid-template-columns: 340px 1fr;
      gap: 72px;
      align-items: start;
    }
    .about__aside {
      position: sticky;
      top: 104px;
    }
  }

  .prose h2:first-child {
    margin-top: 0;
  }

  .prose strong {
    color: var(--ink);
  }

  .name-card {
    overflow: hidden;
    border-top: 4px solid var(--saffron);
  }

  .name-card__fa {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: 3rem;
    line-height: 1.9;
    color: var(--turquoise-strong);
    text-align: left;
  }

  .name-card__en {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: 1.6rem;
    font-weight: 800;
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
  }

  .name-card__note {
    margin: 4px 0 20px;
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    color: var(--muted);
  }

  .facts {
    display: grid;
    gap: 14px;
    margin: 0;
    padding-top: 20px;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
  }

  .facts dt {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 6px;
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--turquoise-strong);
  }

  .facts dd {
    margin: 2px 0 0;
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    color: var(--ink-soft);
  }

  .value__title {
    margin-top: 18px;
  }
</style>
